WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.573 --> 00:00:01.740
DEBI CABRERA: Hey, everyone.

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:06.000
Today, we're talking about
visual user interfaces, Pub/Sub

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.500
Lite, Next '22, and
free cloud training.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.700
I'm Debi Cabrera.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.650
And welcome to "This
Week in Cloud,"

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.010
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.530
At Google Cloud, we're
committed to making

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.490
Artificial Intelligence, or
AI, accessible to everyone

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.280
and easier to harness
for new use cases.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.350
That's why we're
excited to announce

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.400
the general availability of
our intuitive new visual user

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.090
interface for Google
Cloud Speech-To-Text, STT,

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.790
API right in Google
Cloud Console,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:42.480
which makes the API much simpler
and easier for developers

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.410
to use.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:47.040
When you build highly resilient
data analytics pipelines,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.140
difficult tradeoffs are common.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.810
Increasing reliability
can come at a cost.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.660
But then pursuing low costs
can mean more hands-on

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.200
operational management.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:00.000
The Cloud Pub/Sub team wants
to give you the flexibility

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.620
to optimize for
cost, reliability,

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.340
and level of management,
given your workload.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.280
So we're introducing
an additional messaging

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.610
option that balances cost
with high availability.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:16.050
This new Pub/Sub Lite offering
is called "Regional Topics."

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:20.190
Google Cloud is now offering
30 days no-cost access

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:23.670
to Google Cloud Skills Boost,
the definitive destination

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:27.150
for skills development to
complete role-based training.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.950
Choose from eight
learning paths,

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:32.430
including Getting Started with
Google Cloud, Cloud Engineer,

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:36.600
Data Analyst, ML
Engineer, and more.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.250
Hope you're ready
for some excitement

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.340
because Google Cloud Next
returns on October 11

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.680
through October 13 of this year.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.470
Join us for keynotes
from industry luminaries

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.750
and engage live with
Google Developers.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:52.350
Explore dynamic content across
various learning levels,

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.320
and dive deep into
technologies and solutions

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.860
spanning the Google Cloud and
Google Workspace portfolios.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:01.980
You will participate in
breakout sessions, demos,

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.460
hands-on training, and hear from
the world's leading companies

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.920
about their digital
transformation journeys.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.530
You'll have opportunities
to connect with experts,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:14.110
get inspired, and
boost your skills.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:16.630
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.160
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.560
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.460
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:25.470
We'll see you in the cloud.

